WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Let's compare the components that show system messages,

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.600
the messages users see through these components.

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.100
The snackbar, the banner and the dialog can all show messages.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.460
But each one has a different priority, a different level of importance.

5
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:22.060
The dialog has the highest priority when it appears in front of the user, especially a modal dialog.

6
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:27.860
It matters a lot: the user has to focus on it and can't do anything else until they close it.

7
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.560
So that's high priority.

8
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.260
The banner is medium priority: it appears at the top and it's clear,

9
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:40.860
but it doesn't block the content the user is working on, so they don't have to stop and focus on it.

10
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.360
It matters, but not very much,

11
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:50.560
and not as little as the snackbar, which shows at the bottom, disappears again and needs no interaction.

12
00:00:50.560 --> 00:01:00.360
The snackbar disappears on its own, unlike the banner, where I have to tap X, Close or an action to close it, or it stays.

13
00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.860
So the banner stays until I deal with it,

14
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.360
and the dialog also needs an action to close it.

15
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:14.360
So this is a comparison of the components that let me give users messages in my system or product,

16
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:20.360
so I know which component to use for each context, priority and message I want to get across,

17
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.560
and use them without annoying the user or giving them a bad experience.

